To prove this one assembles a collection of the morphisms $\tilde V \to V$ into a finite étale covering and shows that the corresponding morphisms $\tilde V_\lambda \to V_\lambda $ form an étale covering as well (after increasing $\lambda $). Next one uses the injectivity to see that the elements $\tilde\xi _\lambda $ glue (after increasing $\lambda $) and one uses the sheaf property for $F$ to descend these elements to an element of $F(V_\lambda )$.